{"id": "tea:atmatattvaviveka:ksanabhanga", "source": "src:atmatattvaviveka", "location": {"ref": "kṣaṇabhaṅga section"}, "paraphrase": "Against the argument that whatever exists is momentary because existence is causal efficacy and an enduring thing could not produce effects successively, Udayana holds that an enduring thing produces effects in succession as its auxiliary causes come together.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["world-fate", "dispute"], "speaker": "Udayana", "concepts": ["cpt:samagri-without-sakti"], "disputes": ["dsp:momentariness"], "notes": "Chapter-level summary from memory.", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U11-nyaya-vaisesika"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U11-nyaya-vaisesika"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:atmatattvaviveka:structure", "source": "src:atmatattvaviveka", "location": {"ref": "structure of the work"}, "paraphrase": "The self is established by refuting four positions that would exclude it: that everything is momentary; that there are no external objects; that qualities are not different from what has them; and that no self is apprehended.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "dispute"], "speaker": "Udayana", "terms": ["trm:atman"], "concepts": ["cpt:self-nyaya-vaisesika"], "disputes": ["dsp:is-there-a-self", "dsp:momentariness", "dsp:external-objects"], "coverage": ["A5", "G"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U11-nyaya-vaisesika"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U11-nyaya-vaisesika"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
